<speak>I appreciate that. Sometimes I answer because I recognise the caller and do not want to seem rude, even though I am in the middle of something. Then neither person gets a good conversation. I should just say it is not a convenient time. I am better at doing that with business suppliers than with people I know personally. Perhaps it is the family-business habit again, where every relationship feels a bit personal. Anyway, today's arrangement has worked well. Being in a separate room and knowing there was time available made a difference. I did not feel I had to keep watching the door.</speak>